# ThreadSanitizer suppressions, used by the sanitizer test presets (TSAN_OPTIONS).
#
# SQLite's WAL index is shared memory between connections to one file. Readers copy its
# header without a lock, twice, and retry if the copies differ; writers hold file locks
# TSan can't see. So two connections in one process report races inside SQLite on Linux.
# Only SQLite's own wal* functions are named here: our code's races still report.
race:^wal
